<title>NETHERLANDS: Dutch bonds close lower, some blame strong dollar.</title>
<headline>Dutch bonds close lower, some blame strong dollar.</headline>
<text>
<p>---------------------(Snapshot at 1530 GMT)---------------------</p>
<p>* DUTCH STATE LOANS	 PRICES			  BID YIELDS</p>
<p>  June 1999 7.50 pct	106.86/96 (-0.14)	   3.68 (+0.07)</p>
<p>  Feb  2002		   115.08/18 (-0.20)	   4.52 (+0.04)</p>
<p>  Feb  2007 5.75 pct	101.73/81 (-0.26)	   5.51 (+0.04)</p>
<p>  Jan  2023		   115.15/35 (-0.41)	   6.29 (+0.03)</p>
<p>* BUND FUTURE (Sept)	102.66 (-0.33)</p>
<p>  TREASURIES  (Sept)	114.06 (-0.10 vs pvs Dutch close)</p>
<p>* DM/NLG			1.12583 (prev 1.12585)</p>
<p>--------------------------(SPREADS)----------------------------</p>
<p>*DSLs versus Bunds  (pvs close)    *DSL curve     (pvs close)</p>
<p> 5 yr	 +0.01	+0.03	  10-2 yr  182     (186)</p>
<p> 10 yr	-0.07	-0.06	  10-5 yr   99	(99)</p>
<p> Long	 -0.07	-0.06</p>
<p>-------------------------(July 14)-----------------------------</p>
<p>* Dutch bonds close lower after an initial strong start. Downtrend gets in when bund futures start struggling.</p>
<p>* Dealers divided on motive with some blaming firmer dollar and other see investors switching to shares with higher returns.</p>
